# Code: MIT (LICENSE). Text, study-card summaries, tasks and results: CC-BY-4.0 (LICENSE-docs).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Field Shift B0 benchmark (method, tasks, scorer or preliminary
  results), please cite it as below. v0.5.0 results are PRELIMINARY: one repeat
  of three, post hoc scorer v2, prompt v1, keys from our own simulator.
type: software
title: "Field Shift B0: a planted-answer benchmark for farm-advisor agents with a decision tool"
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
authors:
  - alias: Benedek45
repository-code: "https://github.com/Benedek45/field-shift"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - LLM agents
  - tool use
  - crop rotation
  - decision support
  - NASA POWER
  - NASA Space Apps 2026
abstract: >-
  B0 tests whether an agent with a crop-rotation decision tool finds a decisive
  fact in a farm brief and uses it. There are 35 control/planted twin pairs in six
  families (hidden limit, quoted price, field fact, priority order, infeasible
  request, missing data). Keys were computed by the Field Shift simulator
  (fieldshift-v25), not from field truth. v0.5.0 contains the method, the public dev
  tasks, the generator and scorer, and preliminary repeat-0 results for
  anthropic/claude-opus-5-5, opencode-go/gpt-6-luna, opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash and
  opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash in OpenCode 2.3.0.
  AI-use disclosure (NASA Space Apps 2026 rules): the code, task generator, scorer
  and documentation were written with AI coding agents in OpenCode, mainly
  Anthropic Claude Opus 5.5 and OpenAI GPT-6
  Luna, under the team's direction and review. The project idea and the
  benchmark question are the team's. The models listed above are the evaluated
  subjects. The keys are simulator outputs, not language-model outputs.
